00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
so what do we know about what caused the  blast the initial fire broke out  late on tuesday afternoon in the port  the cause of that blaze is still  unconfirmed local media reports pointed  to a  fireworks storage facility and video  capturing the fire showed  popping and colored flashes amid the  smoke  other media reports mentioned welding  work that was taking place in a  warehouse nearby  what we do know is that the fire  triggered a huge  explosion at around 6 pm which struck  with a force  of a 3.5 magnitude earthquake and was  reportedly felt  more than 125 miles away in  cyprus that colossal force  was caused by the explosion of 2750 tons  of ammonium nitrate a highly reactive  chemical  which is being stored unsafely in a  hangar  in the pores the industrial chemical is  normally used  in agriculture as a fertilizer but also  in explosives it's an  oxidizer which means it helps fuel to  burn by drawing oxygen to it  enhancing combustion reactions  in stable conditions it is hard to  ignite but can be detonated  if exposed to heat in a confined space  or contaminated  with other substances the question is  what was it doing there it's believed to  have come from a russian-owned cargo  vessel  flying a moldovan flag  the russo's ship left the black sea port  of batumi  in georgia bound for mozambique in  september 2013  carrying more than 2 700 tons of the  chemical  but it was forced to dock in beirut in  2013  after technical problems where it was  then detained  after failing an inspection by port  authorities  it was eventually abandoned by its owner  and crew  and its potentially lethal cargo  offloaded  to hangar 12 in the port where it has  remained  ever since the head of the port and  customs says  several letters were sent to the  judiciary of the last six years  asking for the material to be removed  but no  action was taken a document believed to  be one of those letters  is circulating on social media it  appears  to request permission from the judiciary  to export the chemical cargo from the  warehouse  an investigation has been announced and  a number of port officials  placed under house arrest the country's  prime minister  has pledged to find those responsible  and punish them
 

